  data: {
    LLM: "Game: Go Fish. Setup: Deal 7 cards (2 players) or 5 cards (3+ players); remainder is Stock (Ocean). Gameplay: On your turn, ask any player for a specific rank you hold at least one card of. If they have it, they give you ALL matching cards and you take another turn. If not, you say 'Go Fish' and draw one card from Stock. If you draw the rank you asked for, show it and get another turn. Complete 'books' (4 of the same rank) and lay them face-up. Game ends when all books are completed. Most books wins.",
    Player: "Ask for ranks you hold, collect books of four, and track opponents' requests to infer their hands.",
    objective: 'Collect the highest number of books (four cards of one rank) by successful asks and stock draws.',
    gameplay: "1. **The Ask**: On your turn, ask any player for a specific rank (e.g., 'Alice, do you have any 3s '). **Rule**: You must already hold at least one card of that rank.\n2. **The Catch**: If they have the cards, they MUST give ALL of them to you. You get another turn.\n3. **The Fish**: If they have none, they say 'Go Fish!'. You draw one card from the Stock. - **Lucky Catch**: If you draw the rank you asked for, show it to everyone and take another turn. - **Miss**: If you draw anything else, your turn ends.\n4. **Books**: When you have 4 of a kind, reveal them and place them face-up in front of you.\n5. **Empty Hand**: If you run out of cards, draw new ones from the stock (usually 1, sometimes 5 depending on house rules).",
    keyRules: [
      'You may ask only for a rank you currently hold at least one of.',
      'A player who is asked must hand over all cards of that rank.',
      'When an ask fails, draw one card; if it matches the requested rank, your turn continues.',
      'As soon as a book is completed, it is laid down and removed from hand.',
    ],
    bonusRuleGuids: [],
    useTrump: false,
    trumpBonusValues: null,
