      dealing: "Deal 7 cards each (for 2 players) or 5 cards each (for 3+ players). The rest form the 'Ocean' (Stock) spread out face-down.",
    },
    turnFlow: "1. **The Ask**: On your turn, ask any player for a specific rank (e.g., 'Alice, do you have any 3s '). **Rule**: You must already hold at least one card of that rank.\n2. **The Catch**: If they have the cards, they MUST give ALL of them to you. You get another turn.\n3. **The Fish**: If they have none, they say 'Go Fish!'. You draw one card from the Stock. - **Lucky Catch**: If you draw the rank you asked for, show it to everyone and take another turn. - **Miss**: If you draw anything else, your turn ends.\n4. **Books**: When you have 4 of a kind, reveal them and place them face-up in front of you.\n5. **Empty Hand**: If you run out of cards, draw new ones from the stock (usually 1, sometimes 5 depending on house rules).",
